## App Context
- Perimenopause symptom tracker
- Multiple users, each with isolated data stored as JSON on their own Google Drive
- Prioritize data privacy and security — never mix user data
- Users log irregularly (not daily); insights and date ranges must account for this

## Google Drive Auth
- Google OAuth app is published (not in testing mode)
- Scopes: drive.file, drive.appdata, userinfo.email
- Current issue: refresh token not being stored; users re-auth when access token expires
- Fix: request offline access, store refresh token in localStorage, silently refresh access tokens
- Keep all auth client-side; no backend server
- Never store tokens in the Drive JSON data file

## Development Environment
- **Platform**: Windows
- Use cross-platform commands where possible
- Path separators: prefer `/` for cross-platform compatibility
- Env vars: use `process.env.VARIABLE`
- File ops: prefer `rimraf` over `rmdir /s`
- Process mgmt: `tasklist` / `taskkill /f /pid`

## Re-onboarding Context
- Project paused several months; read existing code carefully before changing anything
- Check SCALE_CONVERSION_REFACTOR.md and SECURITY_CHECKLIST.md before touching related code
- Prefer small, targeted changes while re-familiarizing with the codebase

